% In terms of robustness, Schmelczer et al. \cite{schmelczerTrustworthyRobustAI2023a} propose ``GreatAI'' to establish best practices for transitioning AI systems from prototype to production, while Chen et al. \cite{chenAIMaintenanceRobustness2023} suggest oversight and assessment throughout the AI lifecycle. Wozniak et al. \cite{wozniakRobustnessTestingIndustrial2023} demonstrate the benefits of data augmentation in improving object detection robustness, but, as emphasized by Hutchinson et al. \cite{hutchinsonAccountabilityMachineLearning2021}, it's crucial to consider the accountability implications of such dataset manipulations. Addressing adversarial attacks, Li et al. \cite{liFrameworkEnhancingDeep2021} enhance neural network resilience to malware, and Liu et al. \cite{liuMultiobjectiveSearchRobust2021} show that optimized architectures perform better under adversarial conditions.

