    \begin{corollary} \em \label{coro:multi_single_alignment}
        Let $\mc{Q}$ be a multi-component BCQ. If {\sf CES} and {\sf Resp} are aligned for $\mc{Q}$, then they are aligned for each of the subqueries built from its components. \boxtheorem
    \end{corollary}

  Example  \ref{ex:prop16} shows that the inverse  of Corollary \ref{coro:multi_single_alignment} does not hold.
\ The positive alignment results we obtained  in this section hold for instances with or without exogenous tuples. However, the  non-alignment results required the existence of exogenous tuples. The absence of exogenous tuples will be investigated in the following section.


    \subsection{Alignment in the Absence of Exogenous Tuples}
    \label{sub:ces-resp_noex}



     The proofs we gave for the non-alignment results obtained so far,  those in Theorem \ref{theo:ces_resp_aligned}(b), appeal to the presence of exogenous tuples.  However, we have to investigate if those results still hold without exogenous tuples.
     \ Actually, we will show now that exogenous tuples are indeed required for the non-alignment result for two classes of queries included in Theorem \ref{theo:ces_resp_aligned}(b): \ For them, {\sf CES} and {\sf Resp} are always aligned.
     \  {\em In this section, we assume that instances do not have exogenous tuples.}

