        For {\sf CES}, we recall that it can be computed using the number of swinging worlds or contingencies according to \red{Equations (\ref{eq:ces_shapley_sw}) and (\ref{eq:ces_shapley_cont})}. As an example, we compute the {\sf CES} of $\tau_{ra} \in R_a$: \ A set $W \subseteq D$ will be a swinging world of $\tau_{ra}$ if: (1) contains a positive number of tuples in $S_a$ and (2) there are only tuples of $R_b$ or $S_b$. Then, $\nit{CE}(D,\mc{Q}_{\sf RS},\tau_{ra}) = \frac{(2^{s_a} - 1)\cdot(2^{r_b} + 2^{s_b} - 1)}{2^{m_2 - 1}}$. Analogously, the CES for the rest of tuples are as follows:
