        \begin{itemize}\item[(1)] $\tau_{sa} \preceq^{\rho} \tau_{sb}$ iff $\tau_{sa} \preceq^\nit{CE} \tau_{sb}$,
        \item[(2)] $\tau_{sb} \preceq^{\rho} \tau_{ra}$ iff $\tau_{sb} \preceq^\nit{CE} \tau_{ra}$, and
        \item[(3)] $\tau_{sa} \preceq^{\rho} \tau_{rb}$ iff $\tau_{sa} \preceq^\nit{CE} \tau_{rb}$.
        \end{itemize}

        For (1), \ notice that $\tau_{sa} \preceq^{\rho} \tau_{sb}$ iff $r_a + s_b \leq r_b + s_a$. Also, $\nit{CE}(D,\mc{Q},\tau_{sa}) \leq \nit{CE}(D,\mc{Q},\tau_{sb})$ iff $2^{s_b + r_a}  - 2^{s_b} \leq 2^{s_a + r_b} - 2^{s_a}$. For both, $r_a + s_b = r_b + s_a$ and $r_a + s_b < r_b + s_a$, the scores are \emph{aligned}, since, in the first case, {\sf Resp} is the same for $\tau_{ra}$ and $\tau_{sb}$ (making the exact value of {\sf CES} irrelevant) and, in the second case, the induced orders are the same.

