        Let $\mc{Q}$ be a BCQ containing at least two atoms $A_R$ and $A_S$, with predicates $R,S$, resp., such that: \ (a) $\nit{Var}(A_R) \cap \nit{Var}(A_S) \neq \emptyset$, \ (b) $\nit{Var}(A_R) \not\subseteq \nit{Var}(A_S)$, and \ (c) $\nit{Var}(A_S) \not\subseteq \nit{Var}(A_R)$. \  There is an instance $D$ with exogenous tuples, such that {\sf Shapley} is not aligned with any of {\sf CES} or  {\sf Resp} on $(\mc{Q},D)$. \boxtheorem
    \end{proposition}

