        \vspace{1mm} \noindent (d) For each atom $U \not \in (\nit{Atoms}(x) \cup \nit{Atoms}(y) \cup \nit{Atoms}(z))$, a tuple is created by replacing all variables in $U$ with a constant $c^\prime$. All tuples created this way will be exogenous.

