\begin{lemma}\label{lem:shrinking-only-red}
At each iteration $t$ of Algorithm~\ref{alg:rec-psme}, only points belonging to $P_{\text{tail}}$ are subjected to shrinking, given that $\alpha < \nicefrac{1}{2}$, $\psi = \frac{1}{10m}$ and $c = \frac{1}{80m}$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
The proof uses induction over iterations. Shrinking happens only if a point's mass in a low-eigenvalue subspace is too large. By carefully tracking how shrinking operates and applying Weyl’s theorem and Lemma~\ref{lem:eigenvalue-without-tail}, we show that only initially bad points (i.e., those in $P_{\text{tail}}$) can cause such violations. Full proof appears in Appendix~\ref{appendix:proof_shrinking-only-red}.
\end{proof}

