\section{Conclusion}
\label{section:conclusion}
The presented framework addresses the challenges of time-varying coverage control in nonlinear constrained dynamic systems by developing a two-layer planner-tracker MPC scheme. This framework integrates optimal trajectory planning with a tracking MPC without terminal ingredients. We rigorously establish guarantees on recursive feasibility, adherence to state and input constraints, and collision avoidance. Furthermore, we ensure convergence to an optimal periodic configuration for periodic density functions. The effectiveness of our approach is successfully validated in hardware experiments on a fleet of four small-scale vehicles.

