\section{CAN LLMS REPLACE HUMANS IN SPECIFICATION REFINEMENT?}\label{subsec:known-vulns}


To stress-test LLMs, we conduct case studies on known cellular attacks to assess how far LLMs are from fully automating specification refinement.
As observed earlier, the bottleneck of LLM-driven specification refinement lies in weakness detection (\fillcrtext), which is the focus of this section.

\input{tabs/known-vulns}

We evaluate \ourmodel on existing attacks.
Since \fillcrtext focuses on identifying weaknesses rather than synthesizing attacks, we decide to separate it: 
1) \ourmodel analyzes potential weaknesses across 10 trials.
2) \texttt{GPT-4o} evaluates each analysis according to~\Cref{box:gpt-verifier}, determining whether combining the discovered weakness with the corresponding threat model sufficiently derives the final attack.
3) We manually validate accepted analyses for reliability.
Following~\citet{al2024hermes}, we examine totally 36 types of existing attacks, collecting relevant specification statements, threat models, and attack descriptions for each.
Specification statements were successfully located for 30 attacks, forming the basis of our case studies, while the remaining 6 were excluded due to reliance on implementation or configuration flaws.


The attack list and results are presented in~\Cref{tab:known-vulns}.
\ourmodel successfully detects all 30 types of attacks.
In comparison, the formal analysis method Hermes~\citep{al2024hermes} identifies 19 of these attacks. 
Representative examples of \ourmodel's responses are shown in \Cref{tab:known-vulns-examples}.
It demonstrates the ability to reason about potential weaknesses diversely, which we attribute to the incorporation of multiple rationales during training.
Remarkably, even the rejected responses provide valuable insights, unveiling other negative consequences with unprotected \textit{RRCRelease} message.
While these results are promising, we also identify key challenges that hinder the direct deployment of LLMs for automated cellular specification refinement.


