To implement the above optimization in practice, we design two variations of CU-HLM that differ in how they set the vocabulary compression level.  
The first is an \textit{offline} approach, which selects a static compression strategy using time-averaged statistical information and applies it throughout all rounds.
The second is an \textit{online} approach, which dynamically adjusts the compression level at each round using only time-varying information available on the device, without requiring access to stochastic distributions or prior statistics.

The complete procedure of CU-HLM is summarized in \textbf{Algorithm}~\ref{algo_1} and illustrated in \figref{fig:11_2}, describing its extended operation beyond U-HLM through the integration of compressed vocabulary transmission.


