\begin{definition}
Polynomial invariants of a loop $\mathcal{L}$ are polynomials that vanish before and after every iteration of $\mathcal{L}$. 
The set $I_{\mathcal{L}}$ of all polynomial invariants for $\mathcal{L}$ is an ideal, called the \emph{invariant~ideal~of~$\mathcal{L}$}.
Let $d \geq 1$, the subset $I_{d,\mathcal{L}}$ of all polynomial invariant for $\mathcal{L}$, of total degree $\leq d$, is called the dth \emph{truncated invariant ideal of $\mathcal{L}$}.
    % is the dth truncated ideal of   $I_{\mathcal{L}}$.
    % For an ideal $I\subset\C[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, the \emph{dth truncated ideal} $I_{d}$ is the set $\{f\in I\mid \deg(f)\leq d\}$. 
\end{definition}



