\begin{abstract}
% We study regret minimization for stochastic linear bandits with heavy-tailed rewards that have finite $(1+\epsilon)$–absolute central moment bounded by $\upsilon$, with $\epsilon\in(0,1]$. 
% We improve both the best known upper bounds and lower bounds with respect to prior work. 
% When $\upsilon=\mathcal{O}(1)$, the best known upper bound of prior work is $\tilde O\!\bigl(d\,T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}}\bigr)$.  While a lower bound matching this scaling has also been reported, its construction was for $\upsilon=d$, and adjusting it to attain $\upsilon=\mathcal{O}(1)$ leads to a lower bound of just $d^{\frac{\epsilon}{1 + \epsilon}} T^{\frac{1}{1 + \epsilon}}$, which is the known regret bound for multi-armed bandits, and is below the upper bound by a factor of $\sqrt d$ even for sub-Gaussian noise setting ($\epsilon=1$).
% We design an experimental design based elimination algorithm with regret
% $\tilde O\!\big(d^{\frac{1+3\epsilon}{2(1+\epsilon)}}\,T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}}\big)$,
% the first bound that is sublinear in dimension ~$d$ whenever $\epsilon<1$.  We also prove a lower bound of
% $\Omega\!\bigl(d^{\frac{2\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}}\,T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}}\bigr)$,
% which strictly improves on the tight heavy-tailed multi-armed bandit lower bound. Moreover, for a finite action set of size~$n$ we obtain
% $\tilde O\!\bigl(\sqrt d\,(\log n)^{\frac{\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}}\,T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}}\bigr)
% \quad\text{and}\quad
% \tilde\Omega\!\bigl(d^{\frac{\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}}(\log n)^{\frac{\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}}\,T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}}\bigr).
% $ upper and lower bounds, respectively.
% Finally, we provide an action-set-dependent upper bound, demonstrating that for several action set geometries, such as $l_p$-norm ball, our algorithm matches the lower bound regret rate.

We study stochastic linear bandits with heavy-tailed rewards, where the rewards have a finite $(1+\epsilon)$-absolute central moment bounded by $\upsilon$ for some $\epsilon \in (0,1]$. We improve both upper and lower bounds on the minimax regret compared to prior work. When $\upsilon = \mathcal{O}(1)$, the best prior known regret upper bound is $\tilde{\order}(d T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}})$.  While a lower with the same scaling has been given, it relies on a construction using $\upsilon = \order(d)$, and adapting the construction to the bounded-moment regime with $\upsilon = \mathcal{O}(1)$ yields only a $\Omega(d^{\frac{\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}} T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}})$ lower bound. This matches the known rate for multi-armed bandits and is generally loose for linear bandits, in particular being $\sqrt{d}$ below the optimal rate in the finite-variance case ($\epsilon = 1$).
We propose a new elimination-based algorithm guided by experimental design, which achieves regret $\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(d^{\frac{1+3\epsilon}{2(1+\epsilon)}} T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}})$, thus improving the dependence on $d$ for all $\epsilon \in (0,1)$ and recovering a known optimal result for $\epsilon = 1$.  We also establish a lower bound of $\Omega(d^{\frac{2\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}} T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}})$, which strictly improves upon the multi-armed bandit rate and highlights the hardness of heavy-tailed linear bandit problems. For finite action sets of size $n$, we derive upper and lower bounds of 
$\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(\sqrt d (\log n)^{\frac{\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}}T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}})$ and
$\tilde\Omega(d^{\frac{\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}}(\log n)^{\frac{\epsilon}{1+\epsilon}} T^{\frac{1}{1+\epsilon}})$, respectively. 
Finally, we provide action set dependent regret upper bounds showing that for some geometries, such as $l_p$-norm balls for $p \le 1 + \epsilon$, we can further reduce the dependence on $d$, and we can handle infinite-dimensional settings via the kernel trick, in particular establishing new regret bounds for the Mat\'ern kernel that are the first to be sublinear for all $\epsilon \in (0, 1]$.
